# Chinese Mahjong — Calls You Say During Play
# answer-mode: choice
# choice-count: 4
# answer-case: insensitive

# Each card plays the spoken Chinese call. The Japanese counterpart is shown
# for pronunciation comparison — pon/chii/kan were borrowed from these hanzi.
# (Chinese mahjong has no Riichi declaration.)

@audio audio/chi.mp3
Chī ・ 吃   (JP: Chii チー)
---
Claim the previous player's discard to complete a sequence (three in a row)

@audio audio/peng.mp3
Pèng ・ 碰   (JP: Pon ポン)
---
Claim any player's discard to complete a triplet (three identical tiles)

@audio audio/gang.mp3
Gàng ・ 杠   (JP: Kan カン)
---
Declare a set of four identical tiles, then draw a replacement

@audio audio/hu.mp3
Hú ・ 胡 / 和   (JP: Ron ロン)
---
Declare a win — completing your hand, e.g. on another player's discard

@audio audio/zimo.mp3
Zìmō ・ 自摸   (JP: Tsumo ツモ)
---
Win on a tile you drew yourself

@audio audio/tingpai.mp3
Tīng pái ・ 听牌   (JP: Tenpai テンパイ)
---
Your hand is ready — one tile away from winning
